<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<rule>
									<description>Generate PAM application password</description>
									<comment xml:space="preserve">This policy is to handle the PasswordCheckOut/CheckIn requests from PAM that are delegated to IDM. This policy would do 
1. Random password generation using a password policy from IDM
2. Setting the password in IDM on the mapped Credential object 
3. Setting the password in PAM on the Credential object
4. Setting the password in PAM on the Referenced object in Credential object
The Credential object can be of any application configured for Password CheckIn/CheckOut in PAM. So the Password Policy used for the random password generation can be different based on the type of application. While creating an Account Domain of type appplication, it's type is determined from the name itself which is suffixed with '_&lt;type&gt;', for e.g., in the name blr-srv1_sap, the application type is 'sap'. This type can be used to create entries the PasswordPolicy Mapping Table. The key would be the application type and it's corresponding value will be the Password Policy DN in slash format which is used for random password genration. If there is no mapping defined for a application type, the default Password policy set on the Driver is used.
NOTE: The application type is case-sensitive.</comment>
									<conditions>
										<and>
											<if-class-name mode="nocase" op="equal">DirXML-PUMCredential</if-class-name>
											<if-operation mode="nocase" op="equal">modify-password</if-operation>
											<if-global-variable mode="nocase" name="enable-password-publish" op="equal">true</if-global-variable>
										</and>
									</conditions>
									<actions>
										<do-set-local-variable name="defaultPasswdPolicyDN" scope="policy">
											<arg-string>
												<token-global-variable name="password-policy-dn" />
											</arg-string>
										</do-set-local-variable>
										<do-set-local-variable name="appType" scope="policy">
											<arg-string>
												<token-xpath expression="appl-type/." />
											</arg-string>
										</do-set-local-variable>
										<do-set-local-variable name="pwdPolicyDN" scope="policy">
											<arg-string>
												<token-map default-value="$defaultPasswdPolicyDN$" dest="PolicyDN" src="AppType" table="..\PasswdPolicyMapping">
													<token-local-variable name="appType" />
												</token-map>
											</arg-string>
										</do-set-local-variable>
										<do-trace-message>
											<arg-string>
												<token-text xml:space="preserve">Generating random password using the password policy </token-text>
												<token-local-variable name="pwdPolicyDN" />
											</arg-string>
										</do-trace-message>
										<do-set-local-variable name="randomPasswd" notrace="true" scope="policy">
											<arg-string>
												<token-generate-password policy-dn="$pwdPolicyDN$" />
											</arg-string>
										</do-set-local-variable>
										<do-append-xml-element expression="." name="operation-data" />
										<do-append-xml-element expression="./operation-data" name="random-password" />
										<do-set-xml-attr expression="./operation-data/random-password" name="is-sensitive">
											<arg-string>
												<token-text xml:space="preserve">true</token-text>
											</arg-string>
										</do-set-xml-attr>
										<do-append-xml-text expression="./operation-data/random-password" notrace="true">
											<arg-string>
												<token-local-variable name="randomPasswd" />
											</arg-string>
										</do-append-xml-text>
										<do-if>
											<arg-conditions>
												<and>
													<if-dest-attr name="DirXML-pumReferenceObject" op="available" />
												</and>
											</arg-conditions>
											<arg-actions>
												<do-trace-message>
													<arg-string>
														<token-text xml:space="preserve">Resetting the password of the referenced object in the Credential object...</token-text>
													</arg-string>
												</do-trace-message>
												<do-set-dest-password class-name="User" when="after">
													<arg-dn>
														<token-dest-attr name="DirXML-pumReferenceObject" />
													</arg-dn>
													<arg-string>
														<token-local-variable name="randomPasswd" />
													</arg-string>
												</do-set-dest-password>
											</arg-actions>
											<arg-actions />
										</do-if>
									</actions>
								</rule>
							